tten approval. Cost and timeline impact documented. No obligation to implement without agreement.\nHandover: handover documents provided if included in scope. Training and ongoing support only if explicitly agreed. Ongoing maintenance requires a separate contract.\n\nNEXUSAI PRICING POLICY (must reflect in Commercials section)\nPricing is value-based, not commodity-based. No fixed single price — always show a RANGE.\nEvery quote depends on four factors: time duration, project complexity (low/medium/high), data and integration load, risk and responsibility. Briefly explain which of these apply to this project.\nDO NOT invent any rupee amounts. Leave all monetary values as [Insert quote]. Final amounts are set at proposal sign-off after internal approval.\nMilestone split (default): 30% Kickoff, 40% Mid, 30% Final — express as [30% of Total], [40% of Total], [30% of Total].\nThird-party API costs, paid AI model usage, cloud infrastructure, and licensing fees are billed separately unless explicitly stated.\nCurrency: INR throughout. All fees exclusive of applicable taxes.\n\nNEXUSAI LEGAL POSITIONING (must reflect in scope/liability/IP sections)\nNature of services: professional AI consulting, design, and implementation. Deliverables are assistive, probabilistic, and data-dependent. No guarantee of commercial, financial, regulatory, or operational outcomes.\nLiability: NexusAI's total liability is limited to fees paid under the specific project. No liability for indirect, incidental, consequential, or punitive damages. No responsibility for third-party system failures, APIs, or platforms.\nIP baseline: Client owns final project deliverables upon full payment. NexusAI retains ownership of pre-existing tools, frameworks, templates, and reusable logic. Reuse of non-identifiable generalized learnings is permitted.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\n- 900–1300 words.\n- Professional tone, not salesy.\n- Sections in order: Title/Cover, Executive Summary, Scope & Deliverables, Out of Sc